    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled in the very heart of Stillorgan Village, this charming three-bedroom semi-detached family home (approx. 110 sq.m.) offers the ultimate in suburban convenience and lifestyle. Exceptional transport links are right at your doorstep, with a pleasant stroll through Clonmore Park connecting you directly to the Luas, complemented by nearby Quality Bus Corridors and direct Aircoach routes. Everything your family needs is within easy reach, from top-tier local primary and secondary schools to vibrant shopping centres, boutique retail, and a flourishing scene of trendy cafes and eateries.\n\nBright and beautifully proportioned, the accommodation features a welcoming entrance hall leading to two generous reception rooms and a bright kitchen overlooking the garden, alongside a convenient ground-floor guest cloakroom. Upstairs, three well-appointed bedrooms and a family bathroom offer comfortable living space for a growing household. Neatly manicured, landscaped gardens welcome you at the front while providing excellent, secure off-street parking.\n\nThe standout feature of this property is its sun-drenched, south-facing rear garden extending nearly 12 metres (40 feet). Perfectly positioned to capture sunlight from dawn to dusk, this private landscaped haven creates an ideal backdrop for outdoor dining, summer entertaining, and everyday relaxation.\n\nOffering incredible future versatility, the property holds exceptional scope to expand to meet your evolving needs. Buyers can easily draw inspiration from neighbouring properties to execute an attic conversion, extend over the existing side garage, or build outwards into the generous rear garden (subject to relevant planning permission), making this an outstanding long-term investment. Also to help future-proof this fantastic home, in summer of 2026 they re-roofed the main dwelling at considerable cost, saving any prospective buyer the outlay for the next generation."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall - 4.2m x 2.1m\nWith accommodation off and stairs to first floor level. Cloakroom off.\n\nCloakroom - \nWith WC & WHB.\n\nLiving Room - 3.95m x 3.75m\nFront facing reception room with coving to ceiling and TV point. Gas fire.\n\nDining Room - 3.4m x 3.3m\nRear facing reception room with a door leading to the rear garden.\n\nKitchen - 3.4m x 2.45m\nFloor and eye level white fitted units. Tiled floor and splashback. Door to rear garden.\n\nLanding - 3m x 2.45m\nWith accommodation and hotpress off.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.8m x 3.5m\nFront facing double bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.35m x 3m\nRear facing double bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.8m x 2.5m\nFront facing bedroom with fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 3.4m x 2.35m\nBath with shower over, toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nGarage - 5m x 2.4m\nWith doors leading from driveway. PLumbed for a washing machine. Gas boiler.\n\nBoiler House - \n\n\nGas boiler. - \n\n\nOutside - \nFront garden with a pillared entrance and a driveway with off street parking and access to the garage. Plants and shrubs. Gated side passage leads to the rear garden which is walled in, approximately 12m in length with plants, trees and shrubs and an envious south facing aspect, perfect for capturing all day sun."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Choice location in the heart of Stillorgan</li><li> South facing orientation</li><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Double glazed windows</li><li> Side entrance</li><li> Garage</li><li> Potential to extend</li></ul>"
      },
